Locked. Full picture: **built-ins (curated) + disk discovery + install pointer** per agent. Let me walk through the design in three passes and confirm after each.

## Section 1 of 3 — Architecture & data model

### Three sources of skills, composed per agent

Every agent's skill list in the picker is `builtins ++ discovered ++ maybeInstallHint`, where each source knows how to answer one question:

| Source | What it answers | Per-agent authority |
|---|---|---|
| **`curatedBuiltins`** (Go map) | "What ships with this agent binary?" | hardcoded in code |
| **`discoverSkills(agent)`** (new adapter) | "What review-adjacent plugin skills are installed on disk right now?" | per-agent `SkillDiscoverer` interface |
| **`installHint`** (Go map) | "If the above two are empty, what should I tell the user to install?" | hardcoded in code |

### Data shapes

```go
type curatedSkill struct {
    Name string // "/review"
    Desc string // "Review changes and find issues"
}

type SkillDiscoverer interface {
    // DiscoverReviewSkills walks the agent's on-disk plugin/skill store and
    // returns anything whose name or description matches review-adjacent
    // keywords. Safe to call on fresh installs (returns nil, no error).
    DiscoverReviewSkills(ctx context.Context) ([]curatedSkill, error)
}

type installHint struct {
    // Human-readable line shown when builtins+discovered are both empty
    // OR as a footer even when some skills exist.
    Message string   // "Install `pr-review-toolkit` with `claude plugin install entireio/pr-review-toolkit`"
    Keywords []string // used only for telemetry/debug, not display
}

// Registry data (initial values):
var curatedBuiltins = map[string][]curatedSkill{
    "claude-code": {
        {"/review",          "Review changes and find issues"},
        {"/security-review", "Scan git diff for security issues"},
        {"/simplify",        "Review recent changes for code quality"},
    },
    "codex":        {{"/review", "Review current changes and find issues"}},
    "gemini-cli":   {}, // no built-in review command
}

var installHints = map[string]installHint{
    "claude-code": {Message: "More review skills: install `pr-review-toolkit` via `claude plugin install …`"},
    "codex":       {Message: "More review skills: install `codex-review-pack` via `codex plugins add …`"},
    "gemini-cli":  {Message: "Install `gemini-code-review` with `gemini extensions install <url>`"},
}
```

Agents implement `SkillDiscoverer` as an optional capability interface (next to the existing `HookSupport`, `Launcher`). Agents that don't implement it get an empty discovery result — same fallback as "no skills found."

### What changes in the picker output

The picker's final output is still a `settings.ReviewConfig{Skills, Prompt}` per agent (no settings shape change from 1009). The new machinery is entirely in how we *build the options list shown to the user*. Settings on disk stay identical to 1009's shape — we're not breaking 1009's backward-compat debt any further.

`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`
Modeling `SkillDiscoverer` as a capability interface (like `Launcher` and `HookSupport` today, `agent.go:258-270`) keeps per-agent install-path knowledge local to each agent package. `review.go` only knows about the interface, never about `~/.claude/plugins` or `~/.codex/` paths. If Factory AI Droid or Copilot ever want in, they implement the interface and register; no changes in review code.
`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`

---

Does section 1 (data model + where the new plumbing lives) look right before I move into the discovery algorithm specifics (how each agent's `DiscoverReviewSkills` actually scans disk and what "review-adjacent" match rule to use)?

